From b0fe7ce175f9963a0796256d00c6206a7612a00e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hapto <alex-88-3@hotmail.fr>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:42:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SpecialEvents-Aura: skip aura scanning when nobody listens

The bundled SpecialEvents-Aura-2.0 rescanned every unit on every
UNIT_AURA/PLAYER_AURAS_CHANGED (with tooltip scans for the player) even
though BigWigs' only consumer, the ZombieFood plugin, is off by default.
In a 40-man Molten Core PerfLog this was ~20s of the 42s BigWigs CPU
time, with PLAYER_AURAS_CHANGED spikes up to 55ms.

Scanning now only happens while some addon is registered for a
SpecialEvents_* aura event; otherwise the cache is marked stale and the
query methods rescan the requested unit on demand. Revision bumped so
this copy wins over identical older copies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WJLQrM2ob1poW3peUyML4T
---
 .../SpecialEvents-Aura-2.0.lua                | 66 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Libs/SpecialEvents-Aura-2.0/SpecialEvents-Aura-2.0.lua b/Libs/SpecialEvents-Aura-2.0/SpecialEvents-Aura-2.0.lua
index d753b7a..19a1398 100644
